From: moonrunnerkc <bradkinnard@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:08:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] test: vendor tiktoken's cl100k_base so the suite runs
 offline

test_explicit_tokenizer_provenance_and_special_markers fetched the
cl100k_base vocabulary from openaipublic.blob.core.windows.net on a cold
cache, so it failed wherever tests run with the network closed
(NameResolutionError in a --network none container).

tests/conftest.py now points TIKTOKEN_CACHE_DIR at tests/fixtures/tiktoken,
which holds the upstream file under the SHA-1 of its URL, the name
tiktoken's cache looks up. tiktoken accepts it only if its SHA-256 equals
the hash it pins (223921b7...). tiktoken's MIT license and SOURCE.txt sit
beside it. Nothing under src/ changes; the cold-offline tokenizer test
still sets its own empty cache.

tests/test_tokenizer_offline.py refuses every fetch, points the default
cache at an empty directory so a warm machine cache cannot satisfy it, and
loads cl100k_base. It fails without the vendored copy (the refused fetch)
and passes with it. Implementation ledger count 1590 -> 1591.

Evidence, ghcr.io/astral-sh/uv:python3.12-bookworm, dependencies prepared
online, suite run as a non-root user with the network closed: main fails
this test and the two pre-commit tests (3 failed, 1581 passed); main with
only the new test fails it as well; with this commit only the two
pre-commit tests fail (1583 passed).


