From bb755d22efbfeb771ed7de46ae09e6390b360d7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moonrunnerkc <bradkinnard@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:08:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] test: run the pre-commit hook tests without a PyPI fetch

The tests declared a local hook with language: python. pre-commit builds
a venv for such a hook and pip-installs a placeholder package into it,
and pip's build isolation fetches setuptools from PyPI, so both tests
failed with the network closed ("No matching distribution found for
setuptools>=40.8.0"). That venv never held tracemantle: online it holds
only pip and pre-commit-placeholder-package, and the hook's entry ran the
tracemantle installed beside the tests, from PATH.

language: system runs that same command without building the venv, so
the tests assert what they asserted before. pre-commit 4.7.0, the version
the container resolves, runs it without a warning.

Evidence, same container as the previous commit: both tests pass with the
network closed; the suite is 1585 passed, 6 skipped, exit 0, with the
network closed and with it open.


Cherry-picked from e4c83d4 onto c37c9d6: the base's hook is still named
skillcheck.
